	  File can be a .json, .xml, .cbor, .uswid, or .pc

config SBOM_AMD_PSP_FW
	bool "Include AMD PSP firmware metadata in SBOM"
	default n
	depends on USE_AMDFWTOOL
	help
	  When enabled, amdfwtool generates a CoSWID (Concise Software
	  Identification) SBOM JSON file for each AMD Platform Security
	  Processor (PSP) firmware blob included in the build.

	  Output files are written to build/sbom/ as
	  amd-pspfw-<firmware-filename>.json.  A Makefile fragment
	  (build/sbom/amd-pspfw-sbom.mk) is also generated so that the
	  SBOM assembly step can incorporate the per-blob tags into the
	  final sbom.uswid.

	  Type classifications follow PSPTool conventions
	  (https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool):
	    - Public key types use a dedicated tag template.
	    - No-header types are skipped (soft fuse is never included).
	    - Wrapped KEK types (0x21, 0x82, 0x84, 0x8d) use a template
	      that stores the raw blob content as the version field.
	    - Key store types (0x50, 0x51) and SEV driver (0x1a, if the
	      $PS1 magic is present) are treated as regular PSP FW.

endif
